! Bismuthene without spin-orbit coupling: the control for bismuthene-soc.
!
! The same cell, cutoffs and k-grid, run collinear with the *scalar*-relativistic
! Bi dataset. Using the scalar dataset rather than the relativistic one with
! lspinorb = .false. is deliberate: the second asks QE to j-average the
! projectors (average_pp), which is a third pseudopotential and not the one in
! either file. Comparing the two runs here therefore compares two published
! datasets that differ in exactly one thing -- whether the j channels were kept
! apart -- which is what "the effect of spin-orbit coupling" means.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 4, celldm(1) = 10.109950, celldm(3) = 1.978248,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 35.0, ecutrho = 280.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Bi 208.98 Bi.pbe-dn-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Bi 0.333333333333 0.666666666667 0.0
 Bi 0.666666666667 0.333333333333 0.0
K_POINTS AUTOMATIC
 12 12 1 0 0 0
